  "lineage": "Created in Dangriga, Belize in the late 1970s-80s by Pen Cayetano and developed by Andy Palacio, Chico Ramos and the Garifuna Kids, electrifying the Garifuna punta rhythm — a fast duple 2/4 with the primero drum's improvised lead over the segunda's steady pulse — by adding electric guitar, bass, turtle-shell idiophones, shakers and drum machine, with call-and-response Garifuna-language vocals at roughly 120-140 BPM for carnival and dance-hall use.",
